<service name="source_script">
  <summary>Build a source tarball by running a package's script on a checkout</summary>
  <description>
    Unpacks the obs_scm source archive, runs a script from the package's obs/
    directory in the checkout with a cleared environment (SRC_DIR, OUT_DIR,
    NAME, VERSION, COMMIT, SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH), and packs the single directory
    the script leaves in OUT_DIR into a reproducible .tar.gz. For upstreams
    whose release tarball is produced by a "dist" step rather than being the
    git tree. Run with mode="manual" after obs_scm; leave out the tar and
    recompress services, the tarball this service writes is the source.
    With the "source" parameter it instead packs a directory of the package
    (copied from obs/ into the work directory), optionally after running the
    script on a copy of it.
  </description>
  <parameter name="archive">
    <description>Glob matching the obs_scm source archive (.obscpio or tar). Exactly one file must match, and its .obsinfo must be present. Give exactly one of "archive" and "source".</description>
  </parameter>
  <parameter name="source">
    <description>Plain name of a directory in the work directory to pack, such as "upgrade-scripts". Requires "output". Symlinks are followed; every mtime is 0.</description>
  </parameter>
  <parameter name="script">
    <description>Script file from the package's obs/ directory. Needs a #! line. Required with "archive", optional with "source" (runs on a copy of the directory).</description>
  </parameter>
  <parameter name="output">
    <description>Tarball file name. Default: "name-version.tar.gz" from the archive's .obsinfo. Required with "source".</description>
  </parameter>
</service>
